The map **`scottLambda`** itself (on carriers **`ScottMap (D × D') D''`** and **`ScottMap D (ScottMap D' D'')`**) preserves directed suprema in the function variable; lubs on Scott maps are computed pointwise (Theorem 3.3).

**Theorem (`preservesDirectedSup`).** **`PreservesDirectedSup scottLambda`** (namespace **`scottLambda`**, [`scottLambda.lean`](scottLambda.lean)).

This is the directed-supremum input to Scott continuity of functional abstraction (Proposition 3.5).
